      "kind": "greeting",
      "start": 0.47,
      "end": 1.68,
      "text": "Hey there, how are you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.24,
      "end": 17.64,
      "text": "Shoot from a corner, standing in a doorway if you can, with the camera at about chest height. That shows the most floor and makes the room feel deeper."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 22.49,
      "end": 29.38,
      "text": "Yes, but don't go too wide, or the walls bend and buyers feel tricked. Keep vertical lines straight by holding the phone level."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 34.06,
      "end": 40.53,
      "text": "Clear the surfaces, hide the cables and the bin, make the bed tight. Less clutter honestly reads as more space."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.89,
      "end": 49.84,
      "text": "Open the curtains and turn every lamp on. Shoot in the late morning, when the light coming in is bright but not harsh."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 54.8,
      "end": 59.22,
      "text": "Good luck with the listing. A bright first photo of the main room will do most of the work."
    }
  ]
